1
00:00:56,220 --> 00:00:58,486
[Conversation with his dad.]

2
00:00:59,170 --> 00:01:02,200
(Happy birthday!)

3
00:01:09,100 --> 00:01:10,533
Oh, Dad.

4
00:01:11,633 --> 00:01:13,233
You got off easy

5
00:01:13,633 --> 00:01:16,300
and left him a mess of a jigsaw puzzle.

6
00:01:42,866 --> 00:01:43,866
Hey.

7
00:01:45,433 --> 00:01:46,633
Why'd you come out here?

8
00:01:47,166 --> 00:01:48,200
Watch your step!

9
00:01:49,033 --> 00:01:50,033
I'm fine.

10
00:01:53,333 --> 00:01:54,333
This way.

11
00:02:37,500 --> 00:02:38,800
Give me one.

12
00:02:39,400 --> 00:02:40,599
You smoke too?

13
00:02:40,600 --> 00:02:41,900
I used to

14
00:02:42,900 --> 00:02:44,300
but I never got hooked.

15
00:02:45,666 --> 00:02:47,100
Then you'd better not.

16
00:02:47,233 --> 00:02:48,866
You might get hooked this time.

17
00:02:57,700 --> 00:02:59,166
Why not come back inside?

18
00:03:00,700 --> 00:03:01,700
Avoiding me?

19
00:03:04,200 --> 00:03:05,200
I'm not.

20
00:03:07,033 --> 00:03:08,766
So something's on your mind?

21
00:03:12,066 --> 00:03:13,100
Not really.

22
00:03:13,900 --> 00:03:15,333
You're putting on a front.

23
00:03:15,933 --> 00:03:16,933
Out with it.

24
00:03:17,033 --> 00:03:18,300
Let me hear it too.

25
00:03:19,733 --> 00:03:20,733
Wanna hear it?

26
00:03:21,433 --> 00:03:22,433
Mm.

27
00:03:35,733 --> 00:03:36,733
Go on.

28
00:03:55,600 --> 00:03:57,700
There's this

29
00:03:57,966 --> 00:03:58,966
friend of mine.

30
00:04:00,666 --> 00:04:02,466
When he was twelve

31
00:04:03,266 --> 00:04:04,700
his parents got divorced.

32
00:04:06,533 --> 00:04:07,733
Then one day

33
00:04:09,066 --> 00:04:10,733
his mom brought a man home.

34
00:04:12,400 --> 00:04:14,333
He thought his life was over.

35
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:18,132
So he tried everything he could

36
00:04:18,133 --> 00:04:19,300
to drive that man out.

37
00:04:20,233 --> 00:04:22,333
He even hurt himself to frame him.

38
00:04:25,333 --> 00:04:27,333
But that man never exposed him.

39
00:04:28,866 --> 00:04:30,133
Later on

40
00:04:30,433 --> 00:04:32,366
he spent six months in prison.

41
00:04:34,066 --> 00:04:35,400
When he got out

42
00:04:35,500 --> 00:04:37,333
he said just one thing to my friend.

43
00:04:45,933 --> 00:04:46,933
I'm sorry.

44
00:04:52,633 --> 00:04:55,265
That man never abused your friend.

45
00:04:55,266 --> 00:04:57,133
So why apologize?

46
00:04:59,666 --> 00:05:01,000
I never got it either.

47
00:05:02,233 --> 00:05:04,166
But when I grew up I finally understood.

48
00:05:05,500 --> 00:05:07,066
That apology

49
00:05:07,333 --> 00:05:09,400
maybe it wasn't meant for my friend.

50
00:05:11,600 --> 00:05:13,500
He'd abused someone else?

51
00:05:15,666 --> 00:05:17,666
Maybe something even worse.

52
00:05:17,866 --> 00:05:18,966
Who knows.

53
00:05:19,233 --> 00:05:20,700
But after that

54
00:05:21,100 --> 00:05:22,766
he never said another word about it.

55
00:05:25,266 --> 00:05:26,333
Still

56
00:05:26,600 --> 00:05:27,600
he gave all his love

57
00:05:27,601 --> 00:05:28,866
to that friend of mine

58
00:05:30,233 --> 00:05:31,565
and became the kind of dad

59
00:05:31,566 --> 00:05:32,800
every kid at school envied.

60
00:05:34,700 --> 00:05:36,665
That friend you're talking about

61
00:05:36,666 --> 00:05:38,366
it wouldn't be you, would it?

62
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:42,866
So it was you.

63
00:05:43,100 --> 00:05:45,100
I never thought you'd hurt yourself.

64
00:05:45,333 --> 00:05:47,232
And a criminal who framed someone.

65
00:05:47,233 --> 00:05:48,633
My crimes back then

66
00:05:49,433 --> 00:05:50,766
went way beyond that.

67
00:05:52,233 --> 00:05:54,033
Then go ahead, tell me...

68
00:05:54,200 --> 00:05:55,465
let me hear all the dirt

69
00:05:55,466 --> 00:05:57,233
on a lowlife like you.

70
00:06:19,500 --> 00:06:20,766
Come on, tell me.

71
00:06:43,686 --> 00:06:44,686
Hello?

72
00:06:44,866 --> 00:06:45,900
Oh, Yong Qi.

73
00:06:46,666 --> 00:06:47,366
What?

74
00:06:47,533 --> 00:06:48,833
You're coming to the cabin?

75
00:06:49,700 --> 00:06:50,700
You're almost here?

76
00:06:51,066 --> 00:06:51,433
Uh.

77
00:06:51,434 --> 00:06:52,565
Okay…

78
00:06:52,566 --> 00:06:53,566
Okay, okay.

79
00:06:55,633 --> 00:06:56,866
Yong Qi's coming?

80
00:06:57,266 --> 00:06:58,266
Mm.

81
00:06:58,400 --> 00:07:00,000
She said she's bringing me wine.

82
00:07:00,800 --> 00:07:02,300
Non-alcoholic wine.

83
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:06,066
You two!

84
00:07:13,500 --> 00:07:15,333
Having a barbecue out here

85
00:07:15,666 --> 00:07:16,766
and you didn't invite me?

86
00:07:18,200 --> 00:07:19,765
We're not having a barbecue!

87
00:07:19,766 --> 00:07:21,166
There's no barbecue here.

88
00:07:21,190 --> 00:07:21,690
Right.

89
00:07:22,133 --> 00:07:23,833
We just came to look around.

90
00:07:24,300 --> 00:07:26,000
Then why the big bonfire?

91
00:07:26,633 --> 00:07:27,865
Song Yi

92
00:07:27,866 --> 00:07:29,132
I've got to say this.

93
00:07:29,133 --> 00:07:30,999
He can't drink right now.

94
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:32,366
If you want a drink,

95
00:07:32,433 --> 00:07:33,633
just tell me.

96
00:07:35,600 --> 00:07:37,199
I've got some

97
00:07:37,200 --> 00:07:39,465
non-alcoholic wine.

98
00:07:39,466 --> 00:07:40,300
Whoa.

99
00:07:40,300 --> 00:07:40,900
Here, take it.

100
00:07:40,900 --> 00:07:41,900
Thanks.

101
00:07:43,010 --> 00:07:45,809
But we... we really
weren't having a barbecue.

102
00:07:45,833 --> 00:07:46,633
Look around.

103
00:07:46,634 --> 00:07:47,666
There's nothing here.

104
00:07:48,666 --> 00:07:50,632
But

105
00:07:50,633 --> 00:07:52,066
I've got some!

106
00:07:52,700 --> 00:07:53,966
Whoa!

107
00:07:56,166 --> 00:07:58,000
That's a huge bag of skewers!

108
00:07:58,500 --> 00:08:00,565
You're the best senior ever!

109
00:08:00,566 --> 00:08:01,566
Amazing.

110
00:08:01,900 --> 00:08:03,000
Really?

111
00:08:03,533 --> 00:08:04,865
We really have skewers?

112
00:08:04,866 --> 00:08:07,000
Who's the big sister who loves you most?

113
00:08:07,266 --> 00:08:09,666
That'd be you, Yong Qi!

114
00:08:10,133 --> 00:08:11,799
Come on now, cheers.

115
00:08:11,800 --> 00:08:12,733
Here, Feiyu.

116
00:08:12,800 --> 00:08:14,933
Cheers!

117
00:08:21,266 --> 00:08:21,900
Oof.

118
00:08:21,900 --> 00:08:22,900
Okay, okay

119
00:08:23,133 --> 00:08:24,165
I'm really done.

120
00:08:24,166 --> 00:08:26,833
Now you know what your senior's made of.

121
00:08:27,666 --> 00:08:28,999
All right, all right.

122
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:30,000
We've all had enough.

123
00:08:30,233 --> 00:08:31,133
Let's head back.

124
00:08:31,133 --> 00:08:32,133
Head back?

125
00:08:32,400 --> 00:08:34,065
We've both been drinking

126
00:08:34,066 --> 00:08:35,066
so who's driving?

127
00:08:35,213 --> 00:08:37,980
I came all this way, so we
should just stay the night.

128
00:08:38,233 --> 00:08:39,699
And I want to hear

129
00:08:39,700 --> 00:08:41,900
the orioles singing at dawn.

130
00:08:43,866 --> 00:08:44,900
Uh.

131
00:08:45,833 --> 00:08:47,565
Let's just head back

132
00:08:47,566 --> 00:08:48,766
I'll get us a driver.

133
00:08:49,100 --> 00:08:51,132
We're way out here in the mountains,

134
00:08:51,133 --> 00:08:52,533
how would you even get one?

135
00:08:54,909 --> 00:08:57,565
You mean you can't get one here?

136
00:08:58,066 --> 00:08:59,066
Out here…

137
00:08:59,633 --> 00:09:01,666
you really can't get a driver.

138
00:09:04,300 --> 00:09:06,033
There's only one bed!

139
00:09:06,286 --> 00:09:07,286
How are we going to sleep?

140
00:09:07,366 --> 00:09:09,833
You think that stumps your big sis?

141
00:09:09,866 --> 00:09:12,000
Guess who takes care of this place.

142
00:09:12,600 --> 00:09:14,100
So how are we sleeping?

143
00:09:14,166 --> 00:09:15,332
This cabin has

144
00:09:15,333 --> 00:09:16,800
a top-notch tent.

145
00:09:17,600 --> 00:09:19,833
Way too good for you two!

146
00:09:20,172 --> 00:09:20,772
So,

147
00:09:21,066 --> 00:09:22,300
I'm assigning spots.

148
00:09:22,533 --> 00:09:24,265
You two sleep inside

149
00:09:24,266 --> 00:09:25,999
I'll pitch a tent outside.

150
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:27,000
How's that gonna work?

151
00:09:27,166 --> 00:09:28,332
You're a girl

152
00:09:28,333 --> 00:09:29,500
and it's not safe out there.

153
00:09:30,033 --> 00:09:31,033
Right.

154
00:09:31,200 --> 00:09:32,700
There are wild boars around here.

155
00:09:32,743 --> 00:09:33,543
Then...

156
00:09:33,567 --> 00:09:34,799
you two take the tent

157
00:09:34,800 --> 00:09:35,766
I'll sleep inside.

158
00:09:35,766 --> 00:09:36,766
Deal.

159
00:09:36,800 --> 00:09:38,333
We'll take one tent each.

160
00:09:38,633 --> 00:09:39,966
There's only one tent.

161
00:09:40,866 --> 00:09:41,866
What?

162
00:09:41,970 --> 00:09:43,702
Then one of you'll sleep with me,

163
00:09:43,733 --> 00:09:45,266
I really don't mind.

164
00:09:47,100 --> 00:09:47,400
Um…

165
00:09:47,566 --> 00:09:48,566
Well…

166
00:09:54,733 --> 00:09:55,500
Fine.

167
00:09:55,500 --> 00:09:56,200
Come on.

168
00:09:56,200 --> 00:09:57,200
Raise your drinks!

169
00:09:57,666 --> 00:09:58,666
Bottoms up!

170
00:10:28,266 --> 00:10:29,400
Xu Feiyu?

171
00:10:51,033 --> 00:10:52,466
You're still not asleep?

172
00:10:53,333 --> 00:10:56,200
I'm… sleeping right now…

173
00:10:58,633 --> 00:10:59,633
Mm.

174
00:12:19,033 --> 00:12:20,033
I'm not cold.

175
00:12:20,033 --> 00:12:21,033
Shh.

176
00:12:21,200 --> 00:12:22,466
Don't talk.

177
00:13:07,600 --> 00:13:08,633
Song Yi.

178
00:13:09,466 --> 00:13:10,100
Hm?

179
00:13:10,300 --> 00:13:11,300
You

180
00:13:12,300 --> 00:13:13,300
you're

181
00:13:14,066 --> 00:13:15,800
pressing into me, it's uncomfortable.

182
00:13:16,500 --> 00:13:17,500
Oh.

183
00:13:17,533 --> 00:13:18,666
Sorry about that.

184
00:13:20,066 --> 00:13:21,100
It's fine.

185
00:13:23,666 --> 00:13:25,833
You're too far away.

186
00:13:26,366 --> 00:13:27,366
I'm cold.

187
00:13:30,233 --> 00:13:31,500
Then I'll move closer.

188
00:13:31,833 --> 00:13:32,833
Mm.

189
00:14:04,066 --> 00:14:05,066
Uh.

190
00:14:05,666 --> 00:14:06,800
You're also...

191
00:14:07,766 --> 00:14:08,766
Don't talk.

192
00:14:09,066 --> 00:14:10,066
Go to sleep.

193
00:14:14,866 --> 00:14:17,100
With us pressed together like this

194
00:14:17,533 --> 00:14:18,966
there's no way I can sleep.

195
00:14:20,700 --> 00:14:22,200
I've got an idea

196
00:14:22,266 --> 00:14:24,166
to take your mind off it.

197
00:14:26,133 --> 00:14:27,400
What idea?

198
00:14:29,066 --> 00:14:31,266
Let me tell you a bedtime story.

199
00:14:33,466 --> 00:14:34,466
Go ahead.

200
00:14:35,766 --> 00:14:36,500
Hmm?

201
00:14:36,700 --> 00:14:39,800
Last month, Yong Qi tried
to sleep with a friend of mine.

202
00:14:42,133 --> 00:14:43,533
You have friends?

203
00:14:43,866 --> 00:14:44,666
Ugh!

204
00:14:44,866 --> 00:14:47,266
Quit throwing off my rhythm.

205
00:14:49,693 --> 00:14:51,126
So what happened next?

206
00:14:52,533 --> 00:14:54,066
So then

207
00:14:54,233 --> 00:14:56,566
my friend spent the night in the hospital

208
00:14:57,333 --> 00:14:58,499
and Yong Qi

209
00:14:58,500 --> 00:15:00,833
got yelled at by my friend's mom all night...
